### Example 4 — Java 8 idioms -> Java 21 idioms

**INPUT (Java 8):**

```java
package com.acme.pricing;

import java.math.BigDecimal;

public class PriceQuote {
    private final String sku;
    private final BigDecimal amount;
    private final String currency;

    public PriceQuote(String sku, BigDecimal amount, String currency) {
        this.sku = sku;
        this.amount = amount;
        this.currency = currency;
    }
    public String getSku() { return sku; }
    public BigDecimal getAmount() { return amount; }
    public String getCurrency() { return currency; }

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object o) {
        if (this == o) return true;
        if (!(o instanceof PriceQuote)) return false;
        PriceQuote that = (PriceQuote) o;
        return sku.equals(that.sku)
            && amount.equals(that.amount)
            && currency.equals(that.currency);
    }
    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        return java.util.Objects.hash(sku, amount, currency);
    }
}

public class DiscountService {
    public BigDecimal apply(PriceQuote q, CustomerTier tier) {
        BigDecimal pct;
        if (tier == CustomerTier.BRONZE) {
            pct = new BigDecimal("0.00");
        } else if (tier == CustomerTier.SILVER) {
            pct = new BigDecimal("0.05");
        } else if (tier == CustomerTier.GOLD) {
            pct = new BigDecimal("0.10");
        } else {
            pct = new BigDecimal("0.15");
        }
        BigDecimal discount = q.getAmount().multiply(pct);
        StringBuilder summary = new StringBuilder();
        summary.append("sku=").append(q.getSku()).append("\n");
        summary.append("amount=").append(q.getAmount()).append("\n");
        summary.append("discount=").append(discount).append("\n");
        Logger.getLogger(DiscountService.class).info(summary.toString());
        return q.getAmount().subtract(discount);
    }
}
```

**OUTPUT:**

### Migration plan
- Convert `PriceQuote` to a `record` — it is an immutable value carrier with no inheritance.
- Replace the `if/else if` cascade with a switch expression.
- Replace `StringBuilder` multi-line construction with a text block (SLF4J handles substitution).
- Replace Log4j 1.x style logging with SLF4J parameterised logging.

### File: src/main/java/com/acme/pricing/PriceQuote.java
```java
package com.acme.pricing;

import java.math.BigDecimal;

public record PriceQuote(String sku, BigDecimal amount, String currency) {}
```

### File: src/main/java/com/acme/pricing/DiscountService.java
```java
package com.acme.pricing;

import java.math.BigDecimal;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;

public class DiscountService {

    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(DiscountService.class);

    public BigDecimal apply(PriceQuote q, CustomerTier tier) {
        var pct = switch (tier) {
            case BRONZE   -> new BigDecimal("0.00");
            case SILVER   -> new BigDecimal("0.05");
            case GOLD     -> new BigDecimal("0.10");
            case PLATINUM -> new BigDecimal("0.15");
        };
        var discount = q.amount().multiply(pct);
        log.info("""
                price quote
                  sku={}
                  amount={}
                  discount={}""",
                q.sku(), q.amount(), discount);
        return q.amount().subtract(discount);
    }
}
```

### Manual follow-ups
- Confirm `CustomerTier` is an enum with exactly `BRONZE / SILVER / GOLD / PLATINUM`. If new tiers exist, the switch expression will fail to compile, which is the desired safety check.
- All callers of `getSku()` / `getAmount()` / `getCurrency()` must change to `sku()` / `amount()` / `currency()`. Search the codebase before merging.

