### Example 5 — Spring 4 XML config + RestTemplate -> Spring 6 Java config + RestClient

**INPUT (Spring 4):**

```xml
<!-- applicationContext.xml -->
<beans xmlns="http://www.springframework.org/schema/beans"
       xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xmlns:context="http://www.springframework.org/schema/context"
       xsi:schemaLocation="...">

    <context:component-scan base-package="com.acme"/>

    <bean id="restTemplate" class="org.springframework.web.client.RestTemplate">
        <constructor-arg>
            <bean class="org.springframework.http.client.HttpComponentsClientHttpRequestFactory">
                <property name="connectTimeout" value="5000"/>
                <property name="readTimeout" value="10000"/>
            </bean>
        </constructor-arg>
    </bean>
</beans>
```

```java
package com.acme.client;

import javax.annotation.PostConstruct;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.springframework.web.client.RestTemplate;

@Service
public class InventoryClient {

    @Autowired
    private RestTemplate restTemplate;

    @Value("${inventory.base-url}")
    private String baseUrl;

    @PostConstruct
    public void init() {
        // header defaults set up here in legacy code
    }

    public Stock getStock(String sku) {
        return restTemplate.getForObject(baseUrl + "/stock/" + sku, Stock.class);
    }

    public Stock reserve(String sku, int qty) {
        ReserveRequest req = new ReserveRequest(sku, qty);
        return restTemplate.postForObject(baseUrl + "/stock/reserve", req, Stock.class);
    }
}
```

**OUTPUT:**

### Migration plan
- Replace `applicationContext.xml` with `HttpClientConfig` Java configuration class.
- Replace `RestTemplate` bean with a `RestClient` bean (Spring 6.1+ idiom).
- Replace `@Autowired` field injection with constructor injection.
- Replace `javax.annotation.PostConstruct` with `jakarta.annotation.PostConstruct`.
- Bind `inventory.base-url` to a typed `@ConfigurationProperties` record.

### File: src/main/java/com/acme/client/HttpClientConfig.java
```java
package com.acme.client;

import java.time.Duration;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import org.springframework.http.client.ClientHttpRequestFactory;
import org.springframework.http.client.JdkClientHttpRequestFactory;
import org.springframework.web.client.RestClient;

@Configuration
public class HttpClientConfig {

    @Bean
    public ClientHttpRequestFactory clientHttpRequestFactory() {
        var factory = new JdkClientHttpRequestFactory();
        factory.setReadTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(10));
        return factory;
    }

    @Bean
    public RestClient restClient(ClientHttpRequestFactory factory) {
        return RestClient.builder()
                .requestFactory(factory)
                .build();
    }
}
```

### File: src/main/java/com/acme/client/InventoryProperties.java
```java
package com.acme.client;

import org.springframework.boot.context.properties.ConfigurationProperties;

@ConfigurationProperties(prefix = "inventory")
public record InventoryProperties(String baseUrl) {}
```

### File: src/main/java/com/acme/client/InventoryClient.java
```java
package com.acme.client;

import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.springframework.web.client.RestClient;

@Service
public class InventoryClient {

    private final RestClient restClient;
    private final InventoryProperties props;

    public InventoryClient(RestClient restClient, InventoryProperties props) {
        this.restClient = restClient;
        this.props = props;
    }

    public Stock getStock(String sku) {
        return restClient.get()
                .uri(props.baseUrl() + "/stock/{sku}", sku)
                .retrieve()
                .body(Stock.class);
    }

    public Stock reserve(String sku, int qty) {
        var req = new ReserveRequest(sku, qty);
        return restClient.post()
                .uri(props.baseUrl() + "/stock/reserve")
                .body(req)
                .retrieve()
                .body(Stock.class);
    }
}
```

### Manual follow-ups
- Add `@ConfigurationPropertiesScan` (or `@EnableConfigurationProperties(InventoryProperties.class)`) to your main application class.
- Delete `applicationContext.xml` after confirming nothing else still references it.
- The legacy `connectTimeout` is not a property on `JdkClientHttpRequestFactory`. If you need it, switch to `HttpComponentsClientHttpRequestFactory` and configure the underlying `HttpClient`.
- The original `@PostConstruct` block was empty in the input — verify nothing was lost in transcription.

### Maven / Gradle dependency changes
- Bump `spring-webmvc` / `spring-boot-starter-web` to a version aligned with Spring Framework 6.2 (Spring Boot 3.3.x).
- Remove `spring-boot-starter-webflux` if it was only added to use `RestTemplate` workarounds — `RestClient` lives in `spring-web`.

